              over
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quaternionic+projective+space"} quaternionic projective space
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℍ
                    %msup
                      %mi P
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{H}P^n
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+projective+space"} complex projective space
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℂ
                    %msup
                      %mi P
                      %mrow
                        %mn 2
                        %mi n
                        %mo +
                        %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{C}P^{2n+1}
              equipped with the map that sends complex lines to the quaternionic lines that they span:
            .maruku-equation
